      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T07:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idle mode is defined as \"The sensor is waiting for requests.\", so I don\u0027t think we can expect the sensor to work properly (detect finger up) after setting such a mode.\n\n\u003e we should call fp_idle() on Zephyr to disable the GPIO IRQ (since FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_MODE_IDLE in all 6 Zephyr drivers only calls *_disable_irq(dev) without exiting detect mode on the sensor):\n\nThat\u0027s an implementation detail that we cannot rely on (and on `ft98xx`, `FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_MODE_IDLE` actually puts the sensor into deep sleep).\n\n\u003e leaving the GPIO IRQ enabled on Zephyr triggers an immediate TASK_EVENT_SENSOR_IRQ wakeup\n\nThat\u0027s not fully true. Whether an interrupt is triggered or not depends on the sensor. From my experience, it\u0027s usually triggered on a finger presence change.",
