      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T04:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Simply skipping `fp_sensor_low_power()` when `FP_MODE_FINGER_UP` is set does not guarantee the sensor stays in detect mode:\n\n1. **Combined modes (`FP_MODE_ANY_CAPTURE | FP_MODE_FINGER_UP`)**: `fp_process_finger()` calls `fp_acquire_image()` (which takes all sensors out of detect mode) and clears `FP_MODE_ANY_CAPTURE`, leaving only `FP_MODE_FINGER_UP`. Because L473 checks `FP_MODE_ANY_WAIT_IRQ`, `fp_configure_detect()` is never called after capture.\n2. **Repeated polls in `FP_MODE_FINGER_UP` on `egis630`**: In `isensor_read_interrupt_type_ec630()`, reading a latched FOD interrupt (`THH` when the finger is still down with CL:9963875) calls `ec630_stop_detect_mode()` (line 1570), putting the sensor into `FP_MODE_STANDBY`. Without calling `fp_configure_detect()` again after `fp_finger_status()`, the sensor is only in detect mode for the first poll and stays in `FP_MODE_STANDBY` for all remaining 100ms polls.\n3. **Skipped `gpio_clear_pending_interrupt` on `!CONFIG_ZEPHYR`**: Gating the `else` block on `!(global_context.sensor_mode \u0026 FP_MODE_FINGER_UP)` skips `gpio_clear_pending_interrupt(GPIO_FPS_INT)` at L489 when `evt \u0026 TASK_EVENT_SENSOR_IRQ` is true and `FP_MODE_FINGER_UP` remains set.\n\nL473 should check `FP_MODE_ANY_DETECT_FINGER` symmetrically with L364/L375:\n```cpp\nif (global_context.sensor_mode \u0026 FP_MODE_ANY_DETECT_FINGER) {\n\tfp_configure_detect();\n#ifdef CONFIG_ZEPHYR\n\tif (!(global_context.sensor_mode \u0026 FP_MODE_ANY_WAIT_IRQ))\n\t\tfp_idle();\n#else\n\tif (evt \u0026 TASK_EVENT_SENSOR_IRQ)\n\t\tgpio_clear_pending_interrupt(GPIO_FPS_INT);\n\tif (global_context.sensor_mode \u0026 FP_MODE_ANY_WAIT_IRQ)\n\t\tgpio_enable_interrupt(GPIO_FPS_INT);\n#endif\n} else {\n#ifndef CONFIG_ZEPHYR\n\tif (evt \u0026 (TASK_EVENT_SENSOR_IRQ))\n\t\tgpio_clear_pending_interrupt(GPIO_FPS_INT);\n#endif\n\tfp_sensor_low_power();\n}\n```",
      "revId": "8ca06a6cfb1c299d696109d11a2bc1c0a0ce104d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
